Goal also requires compliance_certificate_alpha to be available at end. So we must not consume it (i.e., not assign it to any candidate). So we must avoid assign_compliance_certificate actions.

Goal also requires route_task_profile_alpha to be available at end. So we must not consume it (i.e., not attach_task_profile to any candidate). So we must avoid attach_task_profile actions.

Thus we must not use assign_compliance_certificate nor attach_task_profile.

We also need to dispatch shift_candidate_alpha and origin_availability_alpha. To dispatch shift_candidate_alpha, we need to allocate a dispatch slot and vehicle unit to shift_candidate_alpha, then execute_schedule_dispatch. To allocate dispatch slot, we need dispatch_ready shift_candidate_alpha, candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_alpha ?route_task_profile, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha. So we need to have a route_task_profile linked to shift_candidate_alpha. The only route_task_profile available is route_task_profile_alpha. So we must attach it to shift_candidate_alpha (via attach_task_profile). That will consume route_task_profile_alpha (making it unavailable). But we need route_task_profile_alpha available at goal. So we must later detach it (via detach_task_profile) to make it available again. That will be extra steps but okay.

Similarly, to dispatch origin_availability_alpha, we need to allocate dispatch slot and vehicle unit to origin_availability_alpha, then execute_origin_dispatch. For allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate, we need dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha, candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha ?route_task_profile, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_allocated origin_availability_alpha. So we also need to link a route_task_profile to origin_availability_alpha. The only one is route_task_profile_alpha. So we must attach it to origin_availability_alpha as well. But we cannot have two route_task_profile linked to two candidates simultaneously? The predicate candidate_task_profile_linked is a binary relation; multiple candidates can be linked to same route_task_profile? The domain does not forbid multiple candidates linking to same route_task_profile. So we can attach route_task_profile_alpha to both shift_candidate_alpha and origin_availability_alpha. However, attach_task_profile consumes route_task_profile_available (makes it unavailable). So after attaching to both, route_task_profile_alpha will be unavailable. We need to detach it from both at the end to make it available again. That is possible.

